@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-il27-published-figures`
IMPORT `ito-s46-donations`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 46. Row IL-27. Expected values worked by hand from line 1745 before the rules were run; none edited.
-- Amounts for 2026 (the consolidation's note, an aid): minimum 207, absolute ceiling 10,354,816. Credit = rate x min(available, ceiling),
-- ceiling = min(30% of taxable income, 10,354,816); rate 35% for an individual, 23% (s 126(a)) for a body of persons.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — section 46`

`the 2026 amounts` MEANS `the amounts of section 46 that the consolidation's note gives for tax year` 2026

-- Fields: tax year; individual; the donations; taxable income; carried in from 1, 2, 3 years earlier; the s 126(a) rate.
GIVEN `the donations` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `income`       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A donor in a tax year, for section 46`
`an individual in 2026 donating` `the donations` `with taxable income` `income` MEANS
    `A donor in a tax year, for section 46` OF 2026, TRUE, `the donations`, `income`, (`Amounts excess donated in earlier tax years and not yet credited, for section 46` OF 0, 0, 0), 23%

GIVEN `the donations` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `income`       IS A NUMBER
      `one`          IS A NUMBER
      `two`          IS A NUMBER
      `three`        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A donor in a tax year, for section 46`
`an individual in 2026 donating` `the donations` `with taxable income` `income` `and carrying in` `one` `,` `two` `,` `three` MEANS
    `A donor in a tax year, for section 46` OF 2026, TRUE, `the donations`, `income`, (`Amounts excess donated in earlier tax years and not yet credited, for section 46` OF `one`, `two`, `three`), 23%

GIVEN `the donations` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `income`       IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A donor in a tax year, for section 46`
`a body of persons in 2026 donating` `the donations` `with taxable income` `income` MEANS
    `A donor in a tax year, for section 46` OF 2026, FALSE, `the donations`, `income`, (`Amounts excess donated in earlier tax years and not yet credited, for section 46` OF 0, 0, 0), 23%

§§ `The minimum donation and the rate`

-- A donation of 1,000 by an individual with income 200,000 (30% = 60,000, so within the ceiling): 35% x 1,000 = 350.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 1000) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 350
-- Both sides of the minimum: 207 does not exceed 207 (0); 208 does (35% x 208 = 72.8 = 364/5).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 207) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 208) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 364/5
-- A body of persons at the s 126(a) rate of 23%: 23% x 1,000 = 230.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`a body of persons in 2026 donating` (LIST 1000) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 230
-- No donations: nothing.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST ) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 0

§§ `Fork F7 — the minimum on the year's donations together, or each`

-- Two donations of 150: together 300 exceeds 207 (35% x 300 = 105); each is under 207 (0). The default declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 150, 150) `with taxable income` 200000) BECAUSE "section 46(a) does not say whether the minimum donation applies to the donations of the year together or to each donation, and here the readings differ"
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46, reading the minimum as` `the donations of the year together` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 150, 150) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 105
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46, reading the minimum as` `each donation on its own` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 150, 150) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 0
-- 300 and 100: together 400 (140); each, only the 300 counts (105). Declined.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46, reading the minimum as` `the donations of the year together` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 300, 100) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 140
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46, reading the minimum as` `each donation on its own` `, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 300, 100) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 105
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 300, 100) `with taxable income` 200000) BECAUSE "section 46(a) does not say whether the minimum donation applies to the donations of the year together or to each donation, and here the readings differ"
-- One donation: the readings agree, the default answers (1,000 -> 350). Two donations each over the minimum: they agree (500 + 500 = 1,000 -> 350).
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 500, 500) `with taxable income` 200000) EQUALS 350
#ASSERT `section 46 — the reading row IL-27 takes of the minimum` EQUALS `declined where the readings differ`

§§ `The ceiling for credit`

-- Income 100,000: 30% is 30,000. A donation of 50,000: credited on 30,000 -> 10,500; 20,000 remains.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 50000) `with taxable income` 100000) EQUALS 10500
#ASSERT `the donations that remain to be carried forward from the tax year under section 46, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 50000) `with taxable income` 100000) EQUALS 20000
-- A donation exactly at the ceiling (30,000): all credited, nothing remains.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 30000) `with taxable income` 100000) EQUALS 10500
#ASSERT `the donations that remain to be carried forward from the tax year under section 46, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 30000) `with taxable income` 100000) EQUALS 0
-- The absolute ceiling: income 100,000,000 (30% = 30,000,000) but 10,354,816 is lower. A donation of 20,000,000: credited on 10,354,816.
-- 35% x 10,354,816 = 3,624,185.6 = 18120928/5. Remains 20,000,000 - 10,354,816 = 9,645,184.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 20000000) `with taxable income` 100000000) EQUALS 18120928/5
#ASSERT `the donations that remain to be carried forward from the tax year under section 46, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 20000000) `with taxable income` 100000000) EQUALS 9645184

§§ `Sums carried in from earlier years`

-- Income 200,000 (ceiling 60,000). Donated 40,000; carried in 30,000 from a year earlier: available 70,000, credited on 60,000 -> 21,000; remains 10,000.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 40000) `with taxable income` 200000 `and carrying in` 30000 `,` 0 `,` 0) EQUALS 21000
#ASSERT `the donations that remain to be carried forward from the tax year under section 46, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 40000) `with taxable income` 200000 `and carrying in` 30000 `,` 0 `,` 0) EQUALS 10000
-- The same with 5,000 carried in from three years earlier as well: available 75,000, credited 60,000 (21,000); 15,000 remains, and
-- whether the 5,000, in its last year, lapses depends on which sums the ceiling took first: the remainder is declined.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 40000) `with taxable income` 200000 `and carrying in` 30000 `,` 0 `,` 5000) EQUALS 21000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the donations that remain to be carried forward from the tax year under section 46, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 40000) `with taxable income` 200000 `and carrying in` 30000 `,` 0 `,` 5000) BECAUSE "section 46(a) does not say which donations a year's ceiling takes first, and here the choice decides what lapses"
-- A sum from three years earlier that the ceiling has room for: 5,000 + 10,000 donated, income 200,000: all credited (15,000 -> 5,250), nothing remains.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 10000) `with taxable income` 200000 `and carrying in` 0 `,` 0 `,` 5000) EQUALS 5250
#ASSERT `the donations that remain to be carried forward from the tax year under section 46, at` `the 2026 amounts` `, for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST 10000) `with taxable income` 200000 `and carrying in` 0 `,` 0 `,` 5000) EQUALS 0
-- The minimum applies to the year's donations, not to a carried-in sum: nothing donated this year and 1,000 carried in: 350.
#ASSERT `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`an individual in 2026 donating` (LIST ) `with taxable income` 200000 `and carrying in` 1000 `,` 0 `,` 0) EQUALS 350

§§ `Tax years`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit under section 46 at` `the 2026 amounts` `for` (`A donor in a tax year, for section 46` OF 2023, TRUE, (LIST 1000), 200000, (`Amounts excess donated in earlier tax years and not yet credited, for section 46` OF 0, 0, 0), 23%) BECAUSE "row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"
#ASSERT `the amounts of section 46 that the consolidation's note gives for tax year` 2024 EQUALS `The amounts of section 46 in force in the tax year` OF 207, 10354816
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amounts of section 46 that the consolidation's note gives for tax year` 2028 BECAUSE "the consolidation's note gives no amounts for section 46 for this tax year"
